<string id="ui_inv_weapon_system"><text>System links</text></string>
<string id="ui_inv_help_weapon_system"><text>Mass and attachments connect the characteristics: added mass improves stability but slows return; optics and launchers increase aim time and lower readiness. Stance, health, stamina, outfit, artifacts and mastery act during live firing.</text></string>
<string id="ui_inv_weapon_help_header"><text>Weapon characteristics</text></string>
<string id="ui_inv_help_weapon_damage"><text>Base damage before ammunition, distance, hit location and protection.</text></string>
<string id="ui_inv_help_bullet_speed"><text>Higher is flatter shooting and needs less lead.</text></string>
<string id="ui_inv_help_rate_of_fire"><text>Speed of successive shots; high rates are harder to control.</text></string>
<string id="ui_inv_help_magazine"><text>Rounds loaded / capacity; parentheses show a loaded grenade.</text></string>
<string id="ui_inv_help_weapon_resource"><text>Estimated base service life; ammunition and attachments may change it.</text></string>
<string id="ui_inv_help_accuracy"><text>Weapon and base-ammunition precision; higher is better.</text></string>
<string id="ui_inv_help_weapon_control"><text>Recoil-control index. Automatic weapons show single-fire and burst control separately. Attachment mass reduces impulse but slows return; suppressor behavior is calculated separately.</text></string>
<string id="ui_inv_help_ready_speed"><text>Combined readiness: draw 40%, aim 40%, holster 20%. Weapon class sets base aim time; optics and launchers slow it.</text></string>
<string id="ui_inv_help_fire_modes"><text>A is automatic; numbers are single fire or burst length.</text></string>
<string id="ui_inv_wear_per_shot"><text>Wear per shot</text></string>
