<string id="ui_inv_artifact_notes"><text>Artifact notes</text></string>
<string id="ui_inv_pudding_help"><text>Reduces fire/electricity wear on the outfit itself; it does not increase the actor's protection. The current condition and strongest powered copy determine the row.</text></string>
<string id="ui_inv_artifact_handling_help"><text>Current condition scales the listed effect. Powered copies use the strongest individual contribution; totals respect the live recoil cap.</text></string>
<string id="ui_inv_sprint_help"><text>The leading figure is the fresh surge; the trailing figure is the sustained pace. The surge tapers over about five seconds. Moving and standing still restore the reserve at different rates. Requires a powered belt and uses only the strongest copy.</text></string>
<string id="ui_inv_hint_artifact_notes"><text>%c[white]LAlt - %c[default]artifact details.</text></string>
<string id="ui_inv_kolobok"><text>Mutant melee buffer</text></string>
<string id="ui_inv_kolobok_help"><text>Stores a small pool of charges against verified mutant melee hits. The first spent charge starts the shared stage recharge; later charges do not restart it. Stage I/II/III/IV: 1/90s, 1/60s, 2/60s, 2/30s. Requires a powered belt. A charge cancels only the incoming hit packet, not separate scripted effects.</text></string>
<string id="ui_inv_spirit_regen"><text>Health recovery (nominal)</text></string>
<string id="ui_inv_spirit_help"><text>The value above is nominal. Recovery intensifies smoothly as health falls: unchanged above 60%, twice as strong around 42.5%, and up to three times as strong at 25% health or lower. Requires a powered belt.</text></string>
